  "question": {
    "text": "The solution of the differential equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>λ</mi><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> (where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math> is an arbitrary constant). Then, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>λ</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
